#====================================================================
# E319 draft - Validate packaged loadable modules with a private host
#====================================================================

id:                     E319
trigger_tool:           conan|test|runtime|dlopen|libtool
phase:                  packaging|testing|runtime
error_signature:        module(load|path).*(not found|failed)|dlopen.*(failed|undefined symbol)|cannot open shared object file|test.*passed.*without package artifacts

severity:               2
category:               dynamic-module|packaging|runtime-validation|conan
match_keywords:         loadable module, plugin, private host, ABI match, minimal configuration, dlopen, libtool, Conan test_package, destructive negative test, same-source test fixture, FIFO capability probe, slapd, rwm.so
title:                  Validate a packaged loadable module through an ABI-matched private host

root_cause:             A loadable module may expose no standalone headers, executable, or stable entry point that a conventional consumer test can call. Checking only that the shared object exists does not prove that the package contains a compatible loader, resolves runtime dependencies, registers the module, or accepts its configuration. Upstream integration tests may also need same-source backends that are outside the package contract, while a merely writable HarmonyOS path may reject FIFOs required by a daemon harness.
affected_scope:         Conan packages whose primary artifact is a plugin, overlay, provider, backend, or other dynamically loaded module with no independent public API, especially when upstream integration coverage needs build-only same-source fixtures or service-test state with filesystem capabilities beyond ordinary file I/O.
verification_cmd:       Generate a minimal configuration with absolute package paths, run the ABI-matched private host in validation-only mode, and confirm a missing-artifact run fails; then build only the same-source fixtures required by selected upstream entries, capability-probe isolated test storage, execute the entries on target, and verify fixture modules are absent from the final package.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           abi-matched-private-host-validation
rec_description:        Build the module and the smallest supported host in one build graph; retain the host and required configuration data as private package artifacts; generate a minimal runtime configuration from resolved package paths; execute the host's validation-only mode; and pair the positive check with a destructive missing-artifact check. Run applicable upstream coverage separately: build its smallest same-source fixtures only for the test phase, select isolated temporary storage by probing every required operation such as file I/O and FIFO creation, execute and count real target entries, and remove fixture artifacts before packaging. Keep the private host out of public bindirs.
rec_command:            |
  # Generic pattern:
  <package-private-host> <validation-only-options> <generated-minimal-config>
  # OpenLDAP rwm example:
  <package>/libexec/slapd -Tt -f <build>/slapd-rwm.conf
  mkfifo <isolated-test-root>/.fifo-probe
  tests/run -b ldif <selected-rwm-test>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-private-host-test-package

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      upstream-host-fixture-with-exact-revision
fallback_description:   When a minimal host cannot be packaged, use an upstream host fixture built from the exact same source revision and dependency graph, and verify its ABI identity before loading the module. Record why the host is external and keep the test isolated from system installations.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          documented-test-fixture

forbid_1_pattern:       (exists|isfile|find).*(\.so|module).*pass|test.*only.*file.*presence
forbid_1_reason:        File presence does not execute the loader, resolve dependencies, initialize the module, or parse module-specific configuration.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI can pass with an unloadable, ABI-incompatible, or incorrectly packaged module.

forbid_2_pattern:       (/usr|/system|PATH).*(host|daemon)|system.*(host|daemon).*load.*package
forbid_2_reason:        A system host may come from a different build, revision, feature set, or ABI than the packaged module.
forbid_2_consequence:   The test becomes environment-dependent and can either mask incompatibility or fail for reasons outside the package.

forbid_3_pattern:       private.*host.*(bin|bindirs)|publish.*validation.*host.*command
forbid_3_reason:        A validation host retained only to exercise a module is not part of the package's supported public command surface.
forbid_3_consequence:   Consumers may depend on an unintended executable and the narrowly scoped module package silently expands into the full host product.

principles:
